[00:00.54] Bought a house from a man in new york
[00:00.54]从纽约一位老人手里接过这栋房
[00:02.02] This house had four small apartments in it when he got it in '78
[00:02.02]他说七七年得到时，里面有四间小公寓
[00:05.92] Said he had seen children grow old and elderly people die in each little apartment
[00:05.92]见过孩子们在各屋长大，老人们在各门后逝去
[00:10.15] Said he didn't change the wooden floors for sixteen years 'cause he knew where the scuff came from
[00:10.15]整整十六年没换木地板，每道刮痕的来历他都清晰
[00:14.97] We talked for a bit and he took me around the corner and told me everything had gone down, down stream from him
[00:14.97]我们聊了会儿，他领我转过街角，说一切都在流逝，一切都在朝下游去
[00:20.04] Like that cold water of his life had gone up his back, down his front, and around his legs
[00:20.04]像浸透他生命的凉水，漫过后背，淌过前胸，绕过双膝
[00:24.30] And before he could drink any of it, it'd already passed him by
[00:24.30]未等他掬饮一口，早已全然逝去
[00:28.03] I went home after drinkin' with him a bit, made a pallet and a fire on the floor
[00:28.03]同他小酌后回到屋里，我铺开地铺，点燃炉火
[00:31.23] I closed my eyes right there in the middle of one of the coldest nights manhattan had seen all winter
[00:31.23]就在那个曼哈顿罕见的寒夜，我阖上双眼
[00:35.77] I imagined my dog jack and me back home cuttin' through some oklahoman landscape
[00:35.77]想象自己和爱犬杰克回到故乡，穿过俄克拉荷马的旷野
[00:39.54] With greens, and moisture, and heat and finding some stream right there in the clearin'
[00:39.54]满目青绿，湿热氤氲，在林间空地忽见溪流一道
[00:44.20] He jumped, chasin' something naturally, and I just let that water run past my shoulders
[00:44.20]它纵身追逐野物，我则任水流没过肩头
[00:48.20] Under my neck and down to my feet, and down, down stream
[00:48.20]漫过颈侧，淌至脚边，一路朝远方，朝无尽的下游去
[00:52.44] Every good and bad thing that ever happend to me floating down, down stream
[00:52.44]所有悲欢往事都漂浮着，朝远方，朝无尽的下游去
[00:55.82] They're just floatin', the tulsa bars and all the throw up in 'em
[00:55.82]它们就这样漂浮着，塔尔萨酒吧的污痕
[00:58.56] The ducks we killed, the fights we had, the new york 3 a.m.s
[00:58.56]我们射落的野鸭，争吵的夜晚，纽约凌晨三点的光景
[01:01.51] The piano through my neighbors wall and the italian restaurant voices mashin' together through the opposite one
[01:01.51]邻居穿透墙壁的琴声，与对门餐馆意大利语的喧哗混作一团
[01:07.10] My mother's couch that I sang her songs on
[01:07.10]母亲沙发上我曾哼唱的旧曲
[01:09.45] The african desert heat, runnin' from the police in school, and my father's swollen pride
[01:09.45]非洲沙漠的炽热，校园里慌乱的步履，父亲肿胀的傲气
[01:14.15] They're just floatin' by, every woman I had ever loved and every man I have ever called a brother
[01:14.15]它们就这样漂浮而过，我曾爱过的每个女子，我曾称兄的每个男人
[01:18.70] The new year's fireworks and the july fourth's too, every failure and every ugly, little victory
[01:18.70]新年与七月的焰火，每次失败与每次微不足道的胜利
[01:23.18] Screamin' off the grand canyon, and hearin' one of my best friends had gotten into a wreck under some cold, dark western sky
[01:23.18]大峡谷荡回呐喊，挚友陨落于西部寒夜的消息
[01:30.05] My sister laughin', the streets of london, and my band playin' sweet notes and hundred thousand people
[01:30.05]妹妹的笑声，伦敦的街道，曾为千万人奏响的旋律
[01:36.60] I took a big gulp and I wondered if all that water led to more streams, and those led to some big ocean somewhere
[01:36.60]我大口吞咽溪水，想着所有这些水流是否汇向更多溪流，那些溪流又是否奔向某片汪洋
[01:41.73] Prayed all that suffering and all those belly laughs led to some big ocean somewhere
[01:41.73]祈求所有叹息与欢歌，终将抵达某片浩瀚之洋
[01:46.29] Soon as I took that big gulp, my eyes opened to a fire in that livin' room
[01:46.29]就在我大口吞饮的刹那，睁眼却见客厅里火焰升腾
[01:49.54] The fire department came, and hydrant filthy new york water was goin' up my back, down my front and down, down stream
[01:49.54]消防队破门而入，消防栓污浊的纽约水柱冲上后背，漫过前胸，奔涌着，朝无尽的下游去
[01:56.57] And so were we
[01:56.57]而我们，亦随波而去
